  abstract = {Stroke is one of the most common cerebrovascular diseases. Transcranial direct current stimulation (tDCS) has been introduced in the research of rehabilitation treatment of stroke; however, its effect is not clear yet. In this study, we performed the first tDCS study which analyzed different-state (before and after tDCS/sham stimulation) electroencephalogram (EEG) data and brain functional networks of stroke patients to investigate the effect of tDCS on stroke. The results showed a significantly higher brain activity in the beta band after tDCS stimulation. This indicates that tDCS might be an effective method for the treatment of stroke.},
